1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,200
Midnight Marquee premieres globally
in five minutes.

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:11,000
Six things can go wrong tonight: a rights holder
underpaid, an ad slot gone blank,

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,400
a bot ring watching for free, a region
buffering out, an audience quietly leaving.

4
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:20,000
Most studios run six separate tools for these,
and none of them talk to each other.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,500
One question that spans two domains:
playback health, and ad revenue.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Two specialists light up. Neither was
named in the question.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,500
This is the real activity trace: the SQL
each specialist ran against ClickHouse.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,500
Two specialists, two domains, two symptoms
- one root cause.

9
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:46,500
Neither could have said that alone. The playback
agent cannot see ad revenue,

10
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,500
and the ads agent cannot see CDN telemetry.

11
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:55,000
That correlation is the entire reason
this is a fleet and not six demos.

12
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:00,500
In ADK this only works because the specialists
are attached as tools that return their findings.

13
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:05,000
As sub-agents they take over the conversation
and never hand it back.

14
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Now the contract itself. Gemini reads the raw
clause and turns prose into computable terms.

15
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Units at the base rate, units at the escalated
rate, expected versus paid, and the gap.

16
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:24,500
Every number here is re-derivable from the
warehouse. Nothing is a magic constant.

17
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:30,000
That is what makes this forensic accounting
a lawyer could follow, instead of a dashboard.

18
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
One device fingerprint across ninety accounts,
corroborated by impossible travel.

19
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:46,000
The ring is hiding in a realistic crowd.
Fan-out alone is not fraud.

20
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:52,000
And notice it consulted one specialist, not six.
This is a single-domain question,

21
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,000
and the orchestrator routes rather than
firing at everything.

22
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,000
That report was not written for me.
Cloud Scheduler called the fleet on the hour.

23
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,500
Control Room ran a standing brief, two specialists
queried ClickHouse, and it filed a root cause

24
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:14,000
with an alert severity it assigned itself,
while nobody was watching.

25
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
The panel was already full when this
recording started.

26
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:22,500
A CDN node does not fail at a convenient hour.
The trigger is a clock, not a request.

27
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:26,500
The endpoint returns immediately and the fleet
keeps working long after the caller has gone.

28
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:33,000
The ground truth is in the repo. This asserts
every seeded anomaly against the live database,

29
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,500
including that the decoys exist,
so detection is not trivial.

30
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:43,500
And ADK's rubric judge scores the fleet against
23 rubrics from that same ground-truth file.

31
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:48,000
Two of them check the agents do not invent
findings that aren't there.

32
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:54,000
Six specialists, one ClickHouse foundation,
one orchestrator that connects the dots.

33
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Gemini 2.5 on Vertex AI, the Agent Development Kit,
and the official ClickHouse MCP server.

34
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Live, end to end. This is The Backlot.
